+# Gosset
+
+**Gosset** is a general-purpose program for constructing experimental designs, developed by **R. H. Hardin** and **N. J. A. Sloane** at AT&T Bell Labs between 1991 and 2003.
+
+It was placed in the **Public Domain** on August 12, 2017.
+
+## Overview
+
+Gosset can be used to:
+- Find D-optimal, A-optimal, and I-optimal designs.
+- Handle both discrete and continuous variables.
+- Respect complex constraints.
+- Solve packing and covering problems.
+
+It is particularly famous for its use in finding "optimal" points on spheres and other regions.
+
+## Compilation
+
+This version has been slightly modified to compile on modern GCC (fix for `non-constant initializer` and missing headers).
+
+To compile:
+```bash
+gcc -std=gnu89 -fpermissive -w main.c -o gosset -lm
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+Run the `gosset` binary. It acts as an interactive shell.
+First, specify a work directory:
+```
+cd work
+```
+Then you can use commands like `help` to see available topics.
+
+## History
+
+This repository is a mirror of the code available at [neilsloane.com/gosset/](https://neilsloane.com/gosset/).
+The original archive was distributed as a `cpio` file named `codemart.cpio`.
+The version history (as documented in the `changes` file) goes from 1991 (v000) to 2003 (v284).
